  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When fossil fuels&nbsp;are burnt, a variety of pollutants are emitted into the earth&rsquo;s&nbsp;troposphere. Two of the pollutants that are emitted are hydrocarbons (unburnt fuels) and nitric oxide (NO).&nbsp;When these pollutants build up to sufficiently high levels, a chain reaction occurs from their interaction with sunlight in which NO is converted into nitrogen dioxide&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. This&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in turn absorbs energy from sunlight and breaks up into nitric oxide and a free oxygen atom.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>&#957;</mi></mrow></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Oxygen atoms are very reactive and combine with the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in air to produce ozone.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8652;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>NO</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
